commit b6f8fc1244793bfb51df2b80fe4ce9af47b405da

C03: installing or uninstalling a catalog application reads its presence; «en Teams» reads the Steam library (INSTALL1625)

Five open survey rows went to the model without a read. «instala Spotify», «desinstalá Spotify» and «desinstalá Discord» name applications the Windows Start catalog already holds; the product installs nothing by name and uninstalls nothing, so the truthful turn reads app.installed and says the application is already installed, or that it is installed and removing it is done from Windows Settings > Apps, without denying a capability (installed_catalog_application_name; the presence read decides; the argument is the catalog name). «instala Batman Arkham Knight en Teams» ×2 writes Steam as «Teams», as the owner already clarified (H0386, H0522): the Steam library read admits «teams» as the platform and the launch verbs («lanzá X en Steam»), and never replaces the launch of a game the local catalog holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


